  "job_B3.3.17.2_20251003_114701": {
    "text": "TO SANCTE MARTINES M\u00e6SSAN.\nMen \u00f0a leofestan, we magan hwylcum hwega wordum secggean be \u00f0\u00e6re arwyr\u00f0an gebyrdo & be \u00f0on\nW\u00e6s \u00f0\u00e6t Gode swi\u00f0e gecoren man on his d\u00e6dum.\nHe w\u00e6s on Pannania \u00fe\u00e6re m\u00e6g\u00f0e \u00e6rest on woruld cumen, in Arrea \u00f0\u00e6m tune.\nW\u00e6s he hwe\u00f0re in Italia afeded in Ticinan \u00fe\u00e6re byrig.\nW\u00e6s he for worlde swi\u00fee \u00e6\u00feelra gebyrda & godra, w\u00e6ron his yldran hwe\u00f0re f\u00e6der & modor, buta\nW\u00e6s his f\u00e6der \u00e6rest cyninges \u00feegn, & \u00f0a \u00e6tnehstan ge\u00f0eah \u00fe\u00e6t he w\u00e6s cininges \u00feegna aldorman.\n\u00dea sceolde Sanctus Martinus nede beon on his geogo\u00f0hade on \u00f0\u00e6re gefer\u00e6denne cininges \u00f0egna, \u00e6rest\nN\u00e6s na \u00fe\u00e6t he his willan on \u00f0\u00e6m woruldfolga\u00f0e w\u00e6re; ah he sona on his geogo\u00f0e Godes \u00f0eowdom\n\u00dea he w\u00e6s tyn wintre, & hine hys yldran to woruldfolga\u00f0e tyhton ond l\u00e6rdan, \u00f0a fleah he to Godes\n& he \u00fea sona w\u00e6s wuldorlice mid eallum his life ymb Godes \u00feeowdom abisgod.\n\u00d0a he w\u00e6s fiftene wintre, \u00fea nyddon hine hys yldran to\u00f0\u00e6m \u00fe\u00e6t he sceolde woroldlicum w\u00e6pnum\n\u00dea w\u00e6s feower gear \u00e6r his fulwihte \u00fe\u00e6t he woroldw\u00e6pno w\u00e6g, & he hine hwe\u00f0re wi\u00f0 eallum \u00fe\u00e6m\nH\u00e6fde he miccle lufan & ealle w\u00e6rnesse to \u00e6lcum men, & he w\u00e6s swi\u00f0e ge\u00feyldig, & ea\u00f0mod, &\n& \u00f0eah \u00fee he \u00fea gyt on l\u00e6wedum hade beon sceolde, hwe\u00f0re he to\u00f0on w\u00e6rnesse h\u00e6fde on eallum\nW\u00e6s he for his arf\u00e6stum d\u00e6dum eallum his geferum leof & weor\u00f0 & ondrysne, & hie hine ealle\n& \u00f0eah he \u00fea gyt n\u00e6re fullice \u00e6fter o\u00feerre endebyrdnesse gefulwad, ah he w\u00e6s gecristnod, swa ic \u00e6r\nHe wolde \u00fe\u00e6m winnendum fultmian, & earme frefran, & hingrigendum mete syllan, & nacode scrydan,\nGemunde he \u00fe\u00e6t Drihten bebead on \u00fe\u00e6m godspelle, de crastino non cogitare, \u00fe\u00e6t se Godes man ne\nMagon we nu \u00feara arf\u00e6stra d\u00e6da sume gehyran s\u00e6cgan \u00fee he \u00fees eadiga wer, Sanctus Martinus, sona\n\u00d0\u00e6t gelamp sume si\u00f0e \u00fe\u00e6t he ferde mid o\u00ferum cininges \u00f0egnum on \u00f0a burg \u00fee Ambinensus hatte; \u00fe\u00e6t\nW\u00e6s se winter eac \u00fey geare to\u00fe\u00e6s grim \u00fe\u00e6t manig man his feorh for cyle gesealde.\n\u00dea s\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r sum \u00feearfa \u00e6t \u00f0\u00e6m burggeate, s\u00e6t eac nacod, b\u00e6d him \u00fea for Gode hr\u00e6gles & \u00e6lmessan.\n\u00dea ferdan hie ealle for\u00f0 be him & heora n\u00e6nig him to cerran nolde, ne him n\u00e6nigre are gedon.\n\u00d0a ongeat se Godes wer Sanctus Martinus \u00fe\u00e6t Drihten him \u00f0one \u00feearfan geheold, \u00fe\u00e6t he him miltsian\nNyste \u00feeah hwe\u00f0re hw\u00e6t he him don sceolde, for\u00f0on \u00fee he naht elles buton his anfealdne gegyrelan, ah\nGeteah \u00feeah his seax & genam his sciccels \u00fee he him on h\u00e6fde, tosna\u00f0 \u00fea hine ontwa, & healfne sealde\n\u00d0a w\u00e6ron \u00fe\u00e6r manige men \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6t gesawon \u00fe\u00e6t hie hine on \u00fe\u00e6m t\u00e6ldon & bismrodan, \u00fe\u00e6t he his swa\nSume \u00feonne eft \u00fea \u00f0e betran modes w\u00e6ron, & \u00e6nige lufe to Gode h\u00e6fdan, hie sylfe be \u00feon oncu\u00f0on\n\u00d0a w\u00e6s sona on \u00fe\u00e6re \u00e6fterfylgendan niht, \u00fea he se eadiga wer slep, \u00fea geseah he Crist sylfne mid \u00fey\n\u00dea w\u00e6s him beboden geornlicor \u00fe\u00e6t he hine urne Drihten ongeate, & \u00fe\u00e6t hr\u00e6gl \u00fee he \u00e6r \u00fe\u00e6m \u00feearfan\nMox angelorum circumstantium multitudinem; \u00f0a geseah he myccle mengeo engla emb hine Drihten\nW\u00e6s on \u00fe\u00e6re d\u00e6de swi\u00fee cu\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t ure Drihten is swi\u00fee gemyndig \u00fe\u00e6s his cwides \u00fee he sylfa \u00e6r\n& he \u00fea wolde \u00feone cwide getrymman on \u00fe\u00e6re godcundan d\u00e6de, & he hine sylfne to\u00f0on geea\u00f0medde\nQuo uisu uir non in gloriam elatus est; \u00f0a he \u00fea se eadiga wer Sanctus Martinus \u00fea gesih\u00fee geseah, \u00fea\n\u00d0a he \u00fea h\u00e6fde tw\u00e6m l\u00e6s \u00fee twentig wintra, \u00fea gefullode hine mon on \u00f0\u00e6re ciricean endebyrdnesse;\n\u00dea forlet he \u00feone woroldfolga\u00f0, & \u00f0a gewat to Sancte Hilarie \u00fe\u00e6m bisceope, \u00fee on Pictauie \u00fe\u00e6re byrig\n\u00de\u00e6t w\u00e6s swi\u00f0e forem\u00e6re man for Gode & his god w\u00e6s swi\u00f0e gecy\u00f0ed.\n& he \u00fea \u00feysne eadigan wer Sanctus Martinus fulfremedlice on Godes \u00e6 & on Godes \u00feeowdom getyde\nW\u00e6s he swi\u00f0e ge\u00feungen on his \u00f0eawum, & sta\u00f0olf\u00e6st on his wordum, & hluttor & cl\u00e6ne on hie life; &\n\u00dea gelamp \u00e6fter \u00feon \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fees eadiga wer Sanctus Martinus sum mynster getimbrede, & he on \u00f0\u00e6m\n\u00dea gelamp sume si\u00f0e \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r com sum gecristnod man to him, \u00fe\u00e6t he wolde mid his lare & mid his\n\u00dea w\u00e6s he \u00fe\u00e6r dagas wel manige; \u00fea wear\u00f0 he untrum on feforadle.\n\u00dea gelamp on \u00fea tid \u00fe\u00e6t Sanctus Martinus w\u00e6s on sumre fore ealle \u00fery dagas; \u00f0a he eft ham com, \u00fea\n\u00dea he \u00fea Sanctus Martinus \u00fe\u00e6t geseah, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fea o\u00f0re bro\u00f0or ealle swa unrote ymb \u00fe\u00e6t lic utan stondan,\n& him w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6t swi\u00fee myccle weorce \u00fe\u00e6t he swa ungefulwad for\u00f0feran sceolde; getrywde \u00fea hwe\u00f0re\n& eode \u00fea on \u00fea cetan \u00fe\u00e6r se lichoma inne w\u00e6s, & heht \u00f0a o\u00f0re men ut gangan, & \u00fea \u00f0a duru inbeleac\n& hine \u00f0a geb\u00e6d, & hine astreahte ofer leomu \u00fe\u00e6s deadan mannes.\n\u00dea he \u00fea lange hwile on \u00fe\u00e6m gebede w\u00e6s, \u00fea ongeat he \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r w\u00e6s godcundlic m\u00e6gen ondweard, &\n\u00dea w\u00e6s ymb hwile, \u00f0a gefelde he \u00fe\u00e6t se deada man his leomu ealle astyrede, & his eagan upahof &\n\u00dea he \u00fea Sanctus Martinus \u00fe\u00e6t geseah, \u00fea w\u00e6s he swi\u00fee gefeonde, & \u00fea cleopode hlude mid mycelre\n\u00d0a \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fea \u00fea o\u00f0re bro\u00fera gehyrdon \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6r ute w\u00e6ron, \u00f0a eodan hie into him; \u00fea gesawon hie\n& hine man \u00fea sona gefulwade & he feala geara \u00e6fter\u00f0on lifde.\nW\u00e6s \u00feis \u00f0ara wundra \u00e6rest \u00fee \u00fees eadiga wer openlice beforan o\u00ferum mannum geworhte; & \u00fea \u00e6fter\nSwylce eac eft gelamp o\u00feer wundor \u00feissum onlic; he ferde sume si\u00f0e \u00fees eadiga wer to sumes mannes\n\u00dea gehyrde he \u00fe\u00e6r on tune mycelne heaf & wop, & manige cleopodan mid mycelre stefne.\n\u00dea gestod he & ahsode hw\u00e6t seo cleopung w\u00e6re; \u00fea s\u00e6gde him mon \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r w\u00e6re sum man earmlice\n\u00d0a he \u00fea Sanctus Martinus \u00fe\u00e6s mannes dea\u00f0 swa earmlicne gehyrde, \u00f0a w\u00e6s him \u00fe\u00e6t sona swi\u00fee sar\n\u00d0a he \u00fea hwile on \u00f0\u00e6m gebede w\u00e6s, \u00fea f\u00e6ringa wear\u00f0 se deada man cwic eft, & for\u00f0locade, &\n\u00d0a genam Sanctus Martinus hine be his handa, & upheah ar\u00e6rde, & hine l\u00e6dde for\u00f0 to \u00feon cafortune\n\u00d0as wundor & manig o\u00feer \u00e6lmihtig God \u00feurh \u00feysne eadigan wer worhte, \u00e6r \u00feon \u00fee he \u00e6fre bisceop\nAh seo\u00fe\u00fean he \u00feon bisceophade onfeng in Turnan \u00f0\u00e6re byrig, nis n\u00e6nig man \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fea wundor ealle\n& \u00f0eah he \u00fea maran had h\u00e6fde, & eac for worlde ricra beon sceolde, \u00feonne he \u00e6r w\u00e6re, \u00feeh hwe\u00fere\n& he his bisceophad swa gedefelice for Gode geheold swa he hwe\u00fere n\u00e6fde \u00fe\u00e6t m\u00e6gen & \u00fea\nOmnes namque unanimiter cupiebant; Ond ealle men forneah, \u00f0a \u00fee \u00f0yses eadygan weres lif cu\u00feon\nW\u00e6s he for\u00f0on swi\u00fee m\u00e6re geond middangeard, & he manig templ & deofolgyld gebr\u00e6c & gefylde,\n\u00d0\u00e6t gelamp sume si\u00f0e \u00fe\u00e6t he ongan b\u00e6rnan sum deofolgild, \u00fee mid \u00fe\u00e6m h\u00e6\u00f0num mannum swi\u00f0e\n\u00dea stod \u00f0\u00e6r sum nytwyr\u00f0e hus bi \u00fe\u00e6m gilde \u00fee he \u00fe\u00e6r b\u00e6rnan ongan.\n\u00d0a slog se wind \u00feone leg on \u00fe\u00e6t o\u00feer hus, & \u00f0uhte \u00fe\u00e6t hit eal forbyrnan sceolde.\n\u00dea he \u00fea Sanctus Martinus \u00fe\u00e6t geseah, \u00fea arn he sona up on \u00fe\u00e6t hus, & \u00f0a gestod ongean \u00fe\u00e6m lege.\n\u00dea gelamp wundorlic wyrd \u00fe\u00e6t se leg ongan slean & brecan ongean \u00feone wind, & efne swa se wind\n& swa se leg wear\u00f0 ge\u00fereatod \u00feurh Sancte Martines gebedu, \u00fe\u00e6t he n\u00e6nigum o\u00f0rum \u00e6rne sce\u00fe\u00fean ne\nSwilce gelamp eft o\u00feer wunder \u00f0ysum onlic.\nHe com to sumum tune \u00f0e Librassa w\u00e6s haten; \u00f0a w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6r gild \u00fee \u00fea h\u00e6\u00feenan men swi\u00f0e\n\u00d0a wolde he Sanctus Martinus \u00e6lce \u00feinga \u00f0\u00e6t gyld abrecan & gefyllan.\n\u00d0a wi\u00f0stodan him \u00f0a h\u00e6\u00feenan men & hine mid teonan aweg adrifon.\n\u00dea eode he \u00f0\u00e6r rihte big on sume stowe, & hine \u00fea gegyrede mid h\u00e6renum hr\u00e6gle swi\u00fee heardum &\n\u00dea he hit for manna teonan gebrecan ne moste, \u00fea comon \u00fe\u00e6r semninga twegen englas to him\n& cw\u00e6don \u00fe\u00e6t hie God sylf sende \u00fe\u00e6t hie sceoldan \u00fe\u00e6t h\u00e6\u00feene weorod geflyman, & Martine\n\u00d0a eodan hie eft to \u00f0\u00e6m tune, & \u00fe\u00e6t gild gebr\u00e6can & gefyldan eal o\u00fe grund.\n& \u00fea h\u00e6\u00feenan men tolocodan, ah hie hwe\u00fere w\u00e6ron mid godcundum m\u00e6gene to\u00f0\u00e6s swi\u00f0e gefyrhte,\nAh hie ealle to Drihtnes geleafan gecirdon, & hie cw\u00e6dan to him \u00f0\u00e6t se an w\u00e6re so\u00f0 God se \u00fee\nSwylce eac gelamp sume si\u00f0e, \u00f0\u00e6r he sum gild br\u00e6c \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r gearn mycel menigeo to him \u00f0ara\n\u00d0a w\u00e6s heora sum re\u00f0ra & hatheortra \u00f0onne \u00fea o\u00fere; gebr\u00e6gd \u00f0a his sweorde, mynte hine slean.\n\u00dea he \u00fea Sanctus Martinus \u00fe\u00e6t geseah, \u00fea dyde he sona \u00fe\u00e6t hr\u00e6gl of his sweoran, & leat for\u00f0 to \u00f0\u00e6m\n\u00d0a he \u00fea se h\u00e6\u00feena man upr\u00e6hte mid \u00fe\u00e6re swi\u00feran handa, & hine slean mynte, \u00f0a feol he f\u00e6ringa\nSwylce w\u00e6s eft o\u00feer wundor \u00f0\u00e6m onlic.\n\u00de\u00e6t gelamp sume si\u00fee \u00fe\u00e6r he sum deofolgild br\u00e6c & fylde, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r gebr\u00e6gd \u00feara h\u00e6\u00feenra manna\nGelomlic \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feonne w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6r he \u00fea idlan gild br\u00e6c, & him \u00fea h\u00e6\u00f0nan men wi\u00feerwearde w\u00e6ron, \u00fe\u00e6t\nTo\u00fe\u00e6s mihtig he \u00feonne w\u00e6s \u00e6lce untrumnesse to h\u00e6lenne, & to\u00f0\u00e6s myccle gife he \u00fe\u00e6s \u00e6t Gode\nGe \u00fe\u00e6t oft gelamp, \u00feonne man hwylcne d\u00e6l his hr\u00e6gles to untruman men brohte, \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00f0onne \u00feurh\n& \u00fe\u00e6s he w\u00e6s \u00f0onne ealles swi\u00feost to hergenne, \u00fe\u00e6t he n\u00e6fre n\u00e6nigum woruldricum men ne cininge\nUere beatus uir in quo dolus; \u00f0is w\u00e6s so\u00f0lice eadig wer, ne w\u00e6s \u00e6fre facen ne inwid on his heortan,\n& efne heofonlice blisse & gefean mon mihte a on his mode & on his andwleotan ongytan.\nNe gehyrde n\u00e6nig man on his mu\u00fee oht elles nefne Cristes lof & nytte spr\u00e6ce, ne on his heortan buton\nSwa eac \u00fees eadiga wer miccle \u00e6r beforan \u00feone d\u00e6g wiste his for\u00f0fore, & him Drihten \u00fe\u00e6t gecy\u00feed\n\u00d0a wiste he sumne hired on his bisceopscire, \u00fee \u00fea unge\u00few\u00e6re & ungesibbe him betweonum w\u00e6ron,\n\u00d0a he \u00fea h\u00e6fde \u00feone hired gesibbodne \u00fee he \u00fe\u00e6r to ferde, & \u00fe\u00e6r dagas wel manige w\u00e6s, \u00fea he \u00fea eft\n\u00d0a wear\u00f0 he f\u00e6ringa swi\u00fee untrum; \u00f0a heht he him ealle his discipulos to, & him s\u00e6gde \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00fea\n\u00dea w\u00e6ron hie ealle sona unrote, & sarlice geb\u00e6rdon, & \u00feis cw\u00e6don to him: Cur nos, pater, deseris aut\nCuma\u00f0 arisende wulfas, todrifa\u00f0 \u00f0ine heorde; hwa forstande\u00fe hie, gif \u00f0u hie ne scyldest?\nWe \u00fe\u00e6t witon \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t is \u00feines modes willa, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu mote \u00feas world forl\u00e6tan & Crist geseon.\nAh miltsa \u00feu hwe\u00fere us & gemyne \u00feu ure \u00feearfa.\n\u00d0a he \u00fea \u00feas word spr\u00e6c, & he hine ealle wepende geseah, \u00fea weop he eac sylf & his mod w\u00e6s\nW\u00e6s he to\u00fe\u00e6s arf\u00e6st \u00fe\u00e6t him w\u00e6s \u00e6ghwe\u00feer on weorce ge \u00fe\u00e6t he leng from Cristes onsyne w\u00e6re,\nHe \u00fea for\u00f0on Drihtnes willan sohte & \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00f0, Min Drihten, longe ic w\u00e6s nu on \u00f0\u00e6m heardan\nW\u00e6s him \u00e6gwe\u00f0er \u00fe\u00e6m eadigan were ge seo Godes lufu to\u00f0\u00e6s hat & to\u00f0\u00e6s beorht on his heortan,\n& him \u00feonne w\u00e6s eac manna lufu to\u00f0\u00e6s mycel \u00fe\u00e6t him n\u00e6nig gewin her on worlde to lang ne to\n\u00dea w\u00e6s he dagas wel manige mid \u00fe\u00e6re feforadle swi\u00fee gestanden, ah he \u00feeah n\u00e6fre godes weorces ne\n& \u00feonne he reste hine, \u00feonne w\u00e6s his seo \u00e6\u00feeleste r\u00e6st on his earan o\u00fe\u00fee elles on nacodre eor\u00f0an.\n\u00dea b\u00e6don hine his discipulos \u00fe\u00e6t hie mostan huru sume uncyme streownesse him under gedon for his\n& a \u00fe\u00e6r he l\u00e6g, he h\u00e6fde his handa upweardes & mid his eagum up to heofenum locade, \u00feyder his\n\u00d0a b\u00e6dan hine \u00fea Godes \u00feeowas \u00fea \u00f0e \u00f0\u00e6r to him coman, \u00fe\u00e6t hie hine moston on o\u00fere sidan\n\u00dea he \u00fea \u00feus spr\u00e6c, \u00f0a geseah he \u00feone awergdan gast deofol \u00fe\u00e6r unfeor standan; \u00f0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 he to him,",
